{{DISPLAYTITLE: <span style="color: #b300b3;">Cannon Cart</span>}}
{{Protection}}{{MagicWords}}{{ClashofClansLink}}

{{Card Infobox|Cost=5|Rarity=Epic|Type=Troop|Arena=Miner's Mine|ReleaseDate=5 August 2017}}
{{Quote|A Cannon on wheels?! Bet they won't see that coming! At low health, it becomes a Cannon not on wheels.}}

The Cannon Cart is an {{Rarity|Epic}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked from the [[Arenas|Miner's Mine (Arena 15)]]. It spawns a single-target, ground-targeting, medium-ranged, ground [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] with high hitpoints and moderate damage. When its hitpoints are lowered below 50%, it becomes a [[:Category:Building Cards|building]] with a 15-second lifetime. It appears as a [[Cannon]] with a wooden base atop a wooden cart, with a small team-colored ridge at the rear and a large bolted ridge in the center. A Cannon Cart card costs 5 [[Elixir]] to deploy.

==Strategy==
{{Battle Deck with Card|:Category:Battle Decks using the Cannon Cart Card}}
*Since the first form isn't a [[:Category:Building Cards|building]], the Cannon Cart is not a substitute for the [[Cannon]]. It is quite difficult to control when the Cannon Cart enters its second form, so it cannot consistently pull building targeting [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] to a favorable position. Thus, the player should seek other alternatives.
*Despite both forms having a large amount of combined health, the Cart being rendered immobile once its first form has been defeated means that it is best to put the Cannon Cart behind a tank or other high-hitpoint troops such as the [[Giant]], P.E.K.K.A, Giant Skeleton, [[Electro Giant]], [[Goblin Giant]], or the [[Golem]], like glass cannon cards. The tank will absorb all damage and the Cannon Cart will clear away units attacking the tank and eventually the [[:Category:Tower Troop Cards|Crown Tower]]. Keep in mind that this combo is very vulnerable to swarms, so it is advised to bring an area damage spell or troops.
*Both its troop and building form at full health can survive one hit from a [[Fireball]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], P.E.K.K.A, [[Elite Barbarians]], or a charging [[Prince]] if they are all at equivalent levels. If the cart is in its troop form, the Mini P.E.K.K.A. will still fully counter it, but his health will be too low for a threatening counterpush.
*If the player does not need to attack any time soon, they can use [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] to destroy the Cannon Cart's shield when it is placed in the back with the opponent's Crown Tower and force it to start decaying. A [[Lightning]], [[Rocket]], or a Fireball combined with [[The Log]] can all defeat the Cart's first form. Although this is a slight negative [[Elixir]] trade, the tower damage gained is enough to offset this.
*Placing a Cannon Cart in the middle of the opponent's territory when they have one Crown Tower destroyed can be a great strategy. The Cannon Cart's decent range will let it lock on to the remaining Crown Tower in a short time, dealing great damage if left ignored. However, if the opponent expects this, they may play a [[Cards|card]] pre-emptively to stop it, causing the Cannon Cart to be a waste of Elixir. This is easier for them to do at a low cost due to the fact that the Cannon Cart will be in range of both the [[King's Tower]] and the Crown Tower when placed as far forward as possible.
**If the Cannon Cart is placed on the second tile from the river closest to the enemy's Crown Tower, the Cannon Cart will actually be out of range of the King's Tower. This is useful as it'll still quickly lock-on to the Crown Tower, whilst also completely eliminating the King Tower's damage output. However, this comes with the drawback of taking a bit longer to connect, giving your opponent more time to react.
*Mini-tanks or high-damage units like the [[Knight]], [[Dark Prince]], [[Lumberjack]], Elite Barbarians, [[Monk]], [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], [[Sparky]], Battle Healer, [[Executioner]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Bowler]], Prince, P.E.K.K.A, [[Skeleton King]], or the Mini P.E.K.K.A. are great counters to Cannon Cart. They can survive multiple hits while dealing great damage to Cannon Cart, destroying it. However, the Cannon Cart can counter these units with the help of Crown Towers, even being able to stop a [[Mega Knight]] despite his jump attack, [[P.E.K.K.A.]], or a [[Giant Skeleton]], as long as at least two Crown Towers are helping.
*The cheapest card combo to counter a Cannon Cart crossing the river alone is the [[Ice Spirit]] or [[Electro Spirit]] combined with [[Skeletons]] or [[Goblins]]. When it is about to roll within range of the player's Crown Tower, the player should deploy the Ice Spirit/Electro Spirt immediately followed by Skeletons/Goblins. The Ice Spirit/Electro Spirit will tank one shot, freeze/stun it, and the Skeletons/Goblins will damage it down to its second form, where it will then be chipped down by the player's Crown Tower. This is a +3 and a +2 Elixir trade respectively, but it is very delicate; the opponent may use a spell to neutralize the combo, and allow the Cannon Cart to connect to the Tower. Since this is unreactable, the player should keep in mind when they can thwart this combo. Using a different card all of a sudden to counter the Cart can make the opponent react wrongly, spelling something that isn't vulnerable like a Knight or Valkyrie.
*The [[Ice Golem]] is the cheapest single card counter to the Cannon Cart with the help of a Crown Tower, and is harder to work around due to his higher health. For the best results, the Ice Golem should be timed so that he begins distracting the Cart the moment the Crown Tower begins targeting it, and he should be placed in such a way that the Ice Golem's death damage also chips at the cart and slows it.
*Swarm cards like the [[Skeleton Army]], [[Barbarians]], [[Royal Recruits]], the [[Guards]] are effective at countering this card, since the Cannon Cart can only attack one target at a time, causing it to be overwhelmed and destroyed. In the case of the Guards and Recruits, the damage of the Cannon Cart is not enough to destroy their shields in one hit, so they can defend it for longer.
*The Cannon Cart has enough firepower to destroy an equivalent-level [[Goblins|Goblin]] in one hit. It is a good card for clearing away small units one by one so that the rest of a push can follow.
*The Cannon Cart is difficult to redirect due to its long range and its immunity to knockback (besides [[The Log]]), so it can be used to surprise an opponent at the start of the game or when they have little to no Elixir. This is especially devastating if a spell is at the ready to defeat any swarms, one of the simplest methods of dealing with the Cart.
*A Cannon Cart can be strong when paired up with [[Graveyard]] due to its fast movement speed and high combined hitpoints, being able to distract the opponent's tower for a sufficient amount of time.
*The Cannon Cart can be used to counter a [[Goblin Barrel]], due to its ability to one-shot them, letting the Goblins get no more than three hits. However, due to it being a negative Elixir trade, the player should try to counterpush with the Cannon Cart to try and even the Elixir deficit or to try and deal damage to a Crown Tower, as otherwise it is a waste of potential.
*The Cannon Cart's shield hitpoints combined with its normal hitpoints are higher than the entire hitpoints of a [[Battle Healer]]. Because of this, it is a good idea to use it in response to a [[Mortar]] or [[X-Bow]] placed at the bridge. Breaking the shield would not result in the building retargeting and as such, the Cannon Cart will tank more shots for longer.
*The [[Ram Rider]] can easily stop a Cannon Cart. Her attack will slowly kill the first form while her charge will deal massive damage to the second form of the Cannon Cart.

