==History==
2017
*The Cannon Cart was once available in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Cannon Cart 2v2 Draft Challenge]], which started on 28/7/2017. In this [[Tournament|challenge]], gameplay was similar to a regular [[2v2]] Draft Challenge, except that 2 of the players were able to choose who would use the Cannon Cart. If the player achieved at least 8 wins, they obtained the Cannon Cart early.
*From 31/7/2017 through 3/8/2017, the [[Shop]] had a special offer where [[Arenas|Arena]] 10+ players could buy up to 6 Magical [[Chests]] at the normal price that guarantee at least 50% of the Chest's contents to be Cannon Cart.
*The Cannon Cart [[Cards|card]] was generally released on 5/8/2017.
*On 9/10/2017, the [[Version History#Epic Quests Update (9/10/2017)|Epic Quests Update]], increased the Cannon Cart's hitpoints and shield hitpoints by 5%. The same update also fixed a bug where [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] would stop targeting the Cannon Cart or get stuck behind a broken Cannon Cart. In addition, it fixed a bug where the [[Inferno Tower]]'s and [[Inferno Dragon]]'s damage did not reset after breaking the Cannon Cart's shield. This change was reverted on 11/10/2017, in a [[Version History#Maintenance Break (11/10/2017)|maintenance break]].
*On 12/12/2017, the [[Version History#Electrifying%20Update%20(12/12/2017)|Electrifying Update]] reverted the Cannon Cart to its state on 9/10/2017. More specifically, the Inferno Tower's and Inferno Dragon's damage would now reset after breaking the Cannon Cart's shield.
2018
*On 25/4/2018, the [[Version History#Clan%20Wars%20Update%20(25/4/2018)|Clan Wars Update]], changed the death animation of the Cannon Cart. The same update also fixed a bug where the Cannon Cart was not being targeted after losing its shield.
*On 20/6/2018, the [[Version History#Summer%202018%20Update%20(20/6/2018)|Summer 2018 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Cannon Cart from Hog Mountain to Builder's Workshop.
*On 6/8/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/8/2018)|Balance Update]], increased the Cannon Cart's unshielded form's lifetime to 30 seconds (from 20 seconds), decreased the unshielded form's deploy time to 0.15 seconds (from 1 second), and gave it knockback immunity.
*On 3/9/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (3/9/2018)|Balance Update]], decreased the Cannon Cart's range to 5 tiles (from 5.5 tiles).
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]], changed it so that {{Rarity|Epic}} cards start at Level 6 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 8).
*On 5/11/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (5/11/2018)|Balance Update]], decreased the Cannon Cart's hit speed to 1.3 seconds (from 1.2 seconds), and increased its attack time interval to 0.5 seconds (from 0.4 seconds).
2019
*On 28/1/2019, the [[Version History#January%202019%20Update%20(28/1/2019)|January 2019 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Cannon Cart from Builder’s Workshop to Hog Mountain.
*On 4/2/2019, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/2/2019)|Balance Update]], decreased the Cannon Cart's attack time interval to 1.2 seconds (from 1.3 seconds).
*On 1/7/2019, the [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (1/7/2019)|July 2019 Update]], decreased the Cannon Cart's attack time interval to 1 second (from 1.2 seconds), increased its first attack time interval to 0.6 seconds (from 0.5 seconds), increased its range to 5.5 tiles (from 5 tiles), and decreased the damage by 17%. It also increased the hitpoints and shield hitpoints by 1.5%. There was also an unannounced change to the Cannon Cart, an increase to its sight range to 6 tiles (from 5.5 tiles).
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]], added a card render to the Cannon Cart's card info screen.
2020
*On 3/3/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (3/3/2020)|Balance Update]], increased the Cannon Cart's damage by 5%.
2021
*On 30/3/2021, the [[Version History#2021%20Quarter%201%20Update%20(30/3/2021)|2021 Quarter 1 Update]], decreased the Cannon Cart's speed to 60 (from 90), now classified as Medium.
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], decreased the Cannon Cart's unshielded form's attack time interval to 0.9 seconds (from 1 seconds), and its first attack time interval to 0.5 seconds (from 0.6 seconds). It also moved the Arena to unlock the Cannon Cart from Hog Mountain to Legendary Arena.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
2022 
*On 4/10/2022, a [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(4/10/2022)|Balance Update]], decreased the Cannon Cart's hitpoints by 8%.
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Cannon Cart from Legendary Arena to Miner's Mine.
2023 
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
2024
*On 6/8/2024, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/8/2024)|Balance Update]], decreased the Cannon Cart's attack time interval to 0.9 seconds (from 1 second) and its first attack time interval to 0.5 seconds (from 0.6 seconds).
2025
*On 8/1/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (8/1/2025)|Balance Update]] decreased the Cannon Cart's shield hitpoints by 8%, but increased its hitpoints by 0.5%.
*On 5/5/2025, the [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (5/5/2025)|May 2025 Update]] increased the Cannon Cart's hitpoints by 109%, but removed its shield hitpoints.
*On 3/6/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (3/6/2025)|Balance Update]] increased the Cannon Cart's hitpoints by 5%.
*On 30/6/2025, the End of June 2025 Update changed the card description. It used to say: “''A Cannon on wheels?! Bet they won't see that coming! Once you break its shield, it becomes a Cannon not on wheels.''"

